From 0cb65c2d01e8fc3fd3eb6dc68feb1e55fb0d787e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: macbox <macbox@localhost>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 19:40:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] order uses through two imports of the same
 pages with MEMORY_WRITE; keep a remapped memory whose imports follow their
 address

The host_rt_in_place failure (surface_aliases'
a_second_buffer_that_joined_nothing_reads_what_the_first_wrote, AfterRemap
in one command buffer: ~2% stale texels) was not a missing barrier: the
tracker recorded COLOR_ATTACHMENT_OUTPUT/COLOR_ATTACHMENT_WRITE ->
TRANSFER/TRANSFER_READ (and -> COMPUTE/SHADER_READ for the kernel reader),
the same barrier the Made and Rebound arrivals get, which read fresh. They
lie in one import; a buffer made after host_range_remapped imports the pages
anew, a second VkDeviceMemory at its own GPU address, and on ANV (Mesa
26.2.4, Arrow Lake, i915) the pass's color writes stayed in L3 under the
first's address. Measured on the lane, AfterRemap only: src |= MEMORY_WRITE
on those barriers, or dst |= MEMORY_WRITE (both ANV's full flush, the tile
cache's among it): fresh; dst |= MEMORY_READ (every cache invalidated):
still stale.

- host_aliases.rs: each placement notes the import its key lies in
  (import_note: the HostImport's address; 0 not known). A use added for a
  key of another import (a range met, a key of its range in another import,
  a joined buffer made at once with an import of its own) takes MEMORY_WRITE
  among the access types of its reads and writes (apart), so every barrier
  between it and a use of the key it is added for carries ANV's full flush.
  Keys in one import (joined, rebound: the usual display surface) take
  nothing. In-pass barriers mask access types to their subpass's
  dependency, so nothing changes there. Always on: the hazard is the
  driver's, whatever the switch (blorp's color writes through one import
  would meet it too).
- Dedupe after a remap (the join this case escaped): host_range_remapped
  ended every memory it touched, as an import made before may keep the old
  pages. On a driver whose pointer imports follow their address
  (DriverFact::PointerImportsFollowTheirAddress, live-switchable) a memory
  whose live imports are all by pointer now stays (remapped_keeping,
  HostImport::by_pointer): a later buffer over the bytes joins its key and
  lies in its import. ARL's device lacks the fact (not in M2V_ARL_FACTS),
  so on the reference host the barrier above is what fixes it; with
  facts_on=PointerImportsFollowTheirAddress the buffer lies in one import.
- host_rt::orders_images: an image use takes its key's bytes while the
  switch is on and once a texture was made in place under it, so turning
  the switch off keeps ordering those images.

Lanes (Arrow Lake, M2V_LANE_IN_PLACE=1): the failing lane passes with
host_rt_in_place=1 (all three arrivals); the 323-lane set with the switch
on: 301 passed, 22 failed (the 17 linear clear-rounding lanes, the 2 that
assert shadows, the 3 baseline failures; the same messages as before);
off: 320 passed, the 3 baseline failures. With
facts_on=PointerImportsFollowTheirAddress: surface_aliases and the
host_memory remap lanes pass. Runtime unit tests tests::host_aliases (3
new) pass; tests::host_import_counts' remap count follows the fact.

